Installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the WDC Learning Portal

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured the @vercel/speed-insights package following the official Vercel documentation for a Vite + React application.

## Changes Made

### Dependencies
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` v2.0.0 to package.json
- Updated package-lock.json with the new dependency

### Code Changes
Modified: `client/src/App.jsx`
- Imported `SpeedInsights` component from '@vercel/speed-insights/react'
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the App root component, placed alongside the existing `<Analytics />` component

## Implementation Details
Following the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I implemented the React integration pattern which is appropriate for this Vite + React project.

The SpeedInsights component was added to the root App component following the same pattern as the existing Analytics component. This ensures Speed Insights will track performance metrics across all pages of the application.

## Verification
- ✅ Package installed successfully using npm
- ✅ Build completed successfully (vite build)
- ✅ No linting or compilation errors
- ✅ All changes follow existing code patterns and conventions

## Next Steps
Once deployed to Vercel, Speed Insights will automatically begin collecting Core Web Vitals and performance metrics. The data will be available in the Vercel dashboard under the "Speed Insights" tab for this project.

Note: The project already had Vercel Analytics installed, so Speed Insights was added as a complementary tool to provide detailed performance monitoring alongside usage analytics.
